1. `isdigit(s[0]);` : we can use isdigit to check whether a particular character 
    in a string is a digit or not , like `cout << (isdigit(check[1])) << '\n';` and 
    this will output non-zero positive number if that index a digit is present otherwise
    this will return 0 . 
    
    
2. `multiset` : 
	1. multiset is different from set because this allow storing multiple same values also , 
	wherease set allows only unique values , and this also sort all elements in ascending order
	2. `initializing a multiset`: `multiset <int> d;` in this way we can initialize it
	3. `Inserting elements in multiset`:  `d.insert(a);` this way we can insert a value in set 
	or even `multiset <int> d {1,2,3};` this is also valid 
	4. `printing elements of a multiset` :below method we can print all elements of multiset.
	5. ```cpp
	    for(auto &c :d){
	        cout << c << ' ';
	    }
	    ```
	6. `d.erase(x);` : this will erase all occurrences of x in multiset d , `d.erase(d.find(x));` 
	but this will erase only one x and keep other occurrences as it is.
	7. `d.count(x);` : This will give frequency of x in d. 
	8. `multiset<int,greater<int>> d;` : by default multiset sorts elements in ascending order 
	and if you want to sort elements in descending order then use this . 
	9. `d.size()` : this will give us the size of the multiset d . 
	
	
3. `long long sum = accumulate(d.begin(),d.end(),0ll);` : for doing sum of a vector array we can use
    accumulate function but make sure to use `0ll` . To avoid any overflow.
    
    
4. `upper bound and lower bound` : 
	  1. `on which data structure works` : any data structure which provides forward pointer like array , 
	  set , maps ,etc . It is recommended to sort that data structure first so we can get better time 
	  complexity . Data structures which has pointer they return pointer , and which has iterator 
	  it return iterator
	  2. `upper_bound` : If gave x to upper_bound then this will find x+1 means even if x is present 
	  in that data structure this will point to just greater possible element in that data structure 
	  and if that is not possible then it will points to last possible accessible position + 1 that 
	  is where any element doesn't exist.
	  3. `lower_bound` : If gave x then this will return x if x is present otherwise this wil return 
	  x+1 just greater possible element that is present in that data structure and  if that is not 
	  possible then it will points to last possible accessible position + 1 that is where any element 
	  doesn't exist.
	  
	  
5. 	`wanted to access the very first key-value pair without knowing key or value just wanted to take first key-value
    pair after map get sorted either in ascending order by default or we did in descending order` : first create a iterator
    it by `auto it = m.begin();` then `it-> first ` printing this will giving key of the very first key-value pair `it->second`
    this will giving corresponding value of first key-value pair and then if we wanted to access second element then instead 
    of doing `it += 1` do `advance(it,i-1)`.
    	   auto it = m.begin();
        advance(it,i-1);
        cout << (it->first) << (it->second) << '\n';
        
        
6. `Making a string by repeating a particular character ` : `string result (k,'1');` result string will contain 1 k times.
